{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"ac04ddd32c606e5194e06ae6c5a302725839cd217c0772f076e0771892b18ba9","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_c0384c9099d2b5dc2b9d54716ac15a8ac24b6203378626e27b8495700fcd2908","overall_assessment":"The paper is a theoretical and empirical study of neural network expressivity that does not contain a dedicated section on ethics, privacy, or broader societal impact. The use of standard public datasets (MNIST, CIFAR-10) is described without specific licensing or consent documentation, and the visible author metadata includes full names and affiliations. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine compliance with specific venue anonymity policies, plagiarism status, or broader impact requirements.","paper_id":"B1TTpYKgx","paper_identity_sha256":"0d92cec224c6473df7711b96da197598f1df183241e47035ad4db2c216a3a142","prompt_identity_sha256":"971dd331e2a99e2809d06eabdb00bba51da9ca3fd28944c3afd9354a36485b41","raw_response_sha256":"b08f08e4c0d8ad9f97773dd3a360b97ac6f297d1502cfb29d34cc4c11bfb24ae","request_identity_sha256":"2739c7d5a92c5ee76b2b67b454638d8a29b5642e977186b9156a841cbb79ddd5","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"22a4924da1c2f5c40ef296ee9f996ea15acd88cb097cbc207fb9bd0920e5a163","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper focuses on the mathematical properties of neural network expressivity, specifically trajectory length, transitions, and activation patterns. It does not contain a dedicated discussion of ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms to specific populations. The experiments involve standard image classification tasks (MNIST, CIFAR-10), which are generally considered low-risk in terms of direct societal harm or dual-use potential. No specific ethical mitigation strategies or responsible AI considerations are provided in the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-024","SRC-026"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the MNIST and CIFAR-10 datasets for its empirical validation. These are standard, publicly available benchmark datasets in the machine learning community. The text does not provide specific details regarding data licensing, consent, or privacy compliance, nor does it mention any personally identifiable information (PII) or sensitive data. The use of these datasets is consistent with common practice, but the paper lacks explicit documentation of adherence to specific data usage policies or licensing terms.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The provided paper text includes the full names of the authors (Maithra Raghu, Ben Poole, Jon Kleinberg, Surya Ganguli, Jascha Sohl-Dickstein) and their institutional affiliations (Google Brain, Cornell University, Stanford University) in the header. The acknowledgements section also names specific individuals (Samy Bengio, Ian Goodfellow, Laurent Dinh, Quoc Le). While this is standard for published versions, the presence of these identifiers means the text is not anonymized. Without a frozen venue-specific anonymity policy for the submission phase, it is not possible to declare a policy violation, but the visible metadata clearly identifies the authors and their affiliations.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not contain information regarding plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The paper cites prior work appropriately, including a reference to the authors' own previous work (Poole et al., 2016). There is no visible evidence of textual overlap with other submissions or uncredited reuse of material. The absence of evidence in the provided text does not prove originality or the absence of dual submission, but no specific concerns are raised by the visible content.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or any discussion of the societal implications of the research. It also does not mention IRB or ethics approvals, which are typically not required for theoretical studies using public, non-sensitive datasets like MNIST and CIFAR-10. The absence of these elements is noted, but without a frozen policy obligation or specific venue requirement for such statements, the paper cannot be judged as non-compliant based solely on the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"cc602bf82015aee5946fa7aed0d48ad6e025bef4358de1211a93ce8048161913","paper_id":"B1TTpYKgx","paper_ordinal":11,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"b08f08e4c0d8ad9f97773dd3a360b97ac6f297d1502cfb29d34cc4c11bfb24ae","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1TTpYKgx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"e49a8dda722a51b6284c99a58b55e47fb9f19461b1262f94541f8245c2bfaf0b","request_identity_sha256":"2739c7d5a92c5ee76b2b67b454638d8a29b5642e977186b9156a841cbb79ddd5","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":875,"prompt_tokens":16849,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":17724},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"2739c7d5a92c5ee76b2b67b454638d8a29b5642e977186b9156a841cbb79ddd5","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}